==Strategy==
Overall tanky units are highly recommended for this level. The goal is to make your way past the waves of Angel and Zombie support, and then make your way past Daboo from there. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Titans]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island]] all can help a lot both stalling and dealing damage to Daboo; others are [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] at a high level for her [[Special Abilities|ability]] to [[Survive|survive]] a lethal strike and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for his good survivability and DPS.

As for tanky meatshields, common choices are [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]]. Both can be good at tanking and dealing some good DPS to Daboo, but due to their long recharge time you may have to use some research combos like [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] or [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] to be able to spawn them faster. Since Daboo of the Dead is immune to Knockback, Freeze, Slow and Weaken, units that can apply debuffs will not be enough to stop his advance, but they could still help against the support Zombies and Angels. Because of this and Daboo's disgustingly long Omni Strike, it's not recommended that you bring cheap, low-health support against him as most of the common debuffers just walk into Daboo's range, get one hit off, and die.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]]: With resistance to Zombies (Having 65,280 hp without the zombie fruit at lvl 30! That's enough to tank 3 Daboo hits!) and Immunity to slow, this unit was basically designed to fight Daboo and the zombies in the stage, do note he comes a bit short dealing with angels.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Basically Shigong but Angels. The zombies can be a problem and Daboo will most likely halt the process of Ramen. Recommend to use when the angelic waves happen.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Usually the go to options for nuking the Angelic Hippoe waves and the one Angel Gory. Do make sure he has an open space to attack.
*[[Can Can Cat]], *[[Pizza Cat]], and other damagers: If the trio listed above isn’t enough, they can help you against the peons and Daboo himself.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-6 Siege Engine/CAT-8 Behemoth]]: Resilient to Daboo's attacks, allowing them to slowly whittle Daboo down while also clearing or weakening Zombie peons. Can also act as a stalling unit considering Daboo's massive range.
*[[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aethur Ltd./Ultra Atlantis Logistix]]: Insane damage against Zombies and easily replaceable with cheap cost and short cooldown. True Form improves survivability with Survive and Dodge allowing them to completely negate any hits.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: Tanky, cheap and very effective on shredding Daboo's massive health pool as well as controlling the peon with their waves. The quick cooldown also allows them to keep up the pressure without leaving you struggling too long.
*[[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S Lionheart/Tigerclaw]]: Massive damage against Zombies while being strong enough to brave some of Daboo's hits. A very good pick who can put a huge dent in Daboo as well as clear out many of the other peons.
*[[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|Sarukani]]: Does it all, can tank a Daboo hit (32 and up, max COTC antimatter fruit treasures), clears out lesser Zombies effectively, strong against both Zombies and Angels, allowing him to take care of both without much struggle, and can be sent out constantly to wear down Daboo. While he won't carry you entirely, Sarukani can definitely help a lot here.
*[[Seashore Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Seashore Kai]]: Very tanky against Zombies with a quick recharge. Seashore Kai can help out on the frontlines, stalling Daboo while dealing respectable damage. While she might not take him out and needs support against Angels, she can be a great help giving you more time to breathe.
*[[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aegis Garu]]: With his Resistance to all traited enemies, he can tank several Daboo hits before dying, and with the added bonus of zombie killer, this [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusive can really shine.
*[[Bliza (Uber Rare Cat)|Bliza]]: Having 200,000 effective health against Zombies, Omni-strike as well as immunity to slow, they can help take out peons that burrow underneath your frontline, as well as tank hits from Daboo to stop him from advancing.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Balrog Cat]]: Balrog is already amazing against Daboo due to Daboo's very slow attack rate and Balrog's quick recharge, but the peons in this stage are spaced far apart so that Balrog can dish out all of his damage on Daboo without interruption.
*[[High School Kingpin Riki (Uber Rare Cat)|High School Kingpin Riki]]: A lot of strategies require Defense combos, and since Riki provides a 1 slot Defense Sm combo, he's going to be good.
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa, type X]]: Premiere A. Bahamut replacement for this stage, being lvl 30, she can withstand 1 hit from Daboo and quickly shred through angel waves to greatly lower this stage's push potential.
*[[Hanasaka Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ravenous Cherry]]: Ravenous Cherry turns this stage into a cakewalk, as they have over 200,000 base health and Resist both Angels and Zombies on top of that. Combined with their 50% chance to Freeze Zombies And Angels and decent damage, the enemies won't be able to scratch him.
*[[Iz the Dancer (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Alluring Dancer]]: She can can shred Daboo if given the chance. Plus she also works very well against the Angels in this stage.
*[[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Sunrise, Sirius]]: She can tank multiple hits from Daboo, as well as deal considerable damage to the angels as well as zombies in the stage. Her somewhat short cooldown(compared to other Ubers) allows her to be sent out quickly once one dies.

